# API Swagger Rule

- Every API must include complete Swagger decorators.
- Use `@ApiTags()` for every controller.
- Use `@ApiBearerAuth()` only for protected endpoints.
- Add `@ApiOperation()` with meaningful summary and description.
- Use DTOs for all request and response models.
- Every DTO field must have `@ApiProperty()` or `@ApiPropertyOptional()`.
- Add validation decorators (`class-validator`) to all DTO fields.
- Document all path parameters using `@ApiParam()`.
- Document all query parameters using `@ApiQuery()`.
- Document request bodies using `@ApiBody()`.
- Add appropriate success responses (`@ApiOkResponse()`, `@ApiCreatedResponse()`, etc.).
- Add error responses (`400`, `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `500`) with examples.
- Include realistic request and response examples.
- Ensure Swagger documentation always matches the implementation.
- Do not expose internal models, secrets, or database entities in Swagger.